Finally, after almost 15 years of playing nethack and couple of
lurking-years in this newsgroup, I can compose an ascension post...






[Leaving some spoiler space, just in case...]

























Started with only 16 points of intelligence and a spellbook of identify,
which is my favorite starting spell. After some wandering, I got holy
water and a potion of gain ability, which made identifying a bit easier.

The "highlights" were definitely the extra wand of wishing in Sokoban, and
a huge, four-grave bones collection in Minetown, with a co-aligned altar.
After a bit of identifying, canceling and sacrifying I had an excellent
collection of whatever I thought I needed. As I'm very familiar with my
stupid mistakes made in past games, I genocided L- and ;-classes right
away.

Well, everything went very smoothly, as I had a good collection of spells
(all bones were old wizards). Until the castle... A ki-rin created some
monsters around me in the left-side maze, and of course there were one
master mind flayer. Didn't remember the non-teleportability of the
level... After sneaking away in a very stupid condition, I had to
re-identify most of my stuff. That was easy, but I was very scared about
how much I would remember of the levels on my way back. As I had found two
magic lamps, and was about to get my second WoW, I didn't hesitate to
spoil myself with a blessed spellbook of magic mapping. Needless to
mention, also h-class was history after this incident (got plenty of magic
markers from bones as well).

Magic mapping made Gehennom quite easy, until I hit another bones level
between Juiblex's and Baalzebub's. Previous player had made some major
mistakes, and there I was, dancing with Dispater, Yeenoghu, Orcus and 
Juiblex. That was very close to DYWYPI. However, I acquired the Demonbane, 
and after some stair-running, I was able to defeat all of those nasty beings.

After the demon convention, everything went smoothly again. I was lucky
enough to avoid all other Riders except Pestilence, and my first choice
was the correct one on the Astral Plane. (I was about to turn back from
the high altar room's door when there seemed to be only Ptah's
priestesses, but then I saw Thoth's and Moloch's as well, so I realized
they are all mixed up...)

Well, I used 12 wishes and genocided three whole character classes for 
this ascension, so there's still room for better results...

